To achieve this, you can use HTML and CSS to position the SVG icon on the right side of the input field and make it clickable. Here is an example of how you can do this:

1. Create an HTML file and include the SVG icon for the reading glass.
2. Position the SVG icon to the right of the input field.
3. Add an `onclick` event to the SVG icon that triggers a JavaScript function when clicked.

Here is an example:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Clickable SVG Icon</title>
    <style>
        .input-with-icon {
